    "title": "City of Wilmington signs historical preservation impact agreement for Cape Fear Memorial Bridge replacement - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By WHQR ,\n8 hours ago That’s a multi-agency agreement led by the Federal Highway Administration. A PA is meant to satisfy requirements set by Section 106, also known as the National Historic Preservation Act of 1966. That’s a federal law that requires officials to analyze a project's impact on historical properties and make a plan to mitigate it. Read full article",
